            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "`MiniSessions.write()` writes current session (specified in `v:this_session`). This is basically what [is done on `VimLeavePre`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/fc95760d5dd8303679ac21e9bb8bf6dab13558ba/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L81). Is this what you are looking for?\r\n\r\nI don't think 'mini.starter' should do any saving upon opening. Probably the best way here is to use manual command for opening Starter buffer or on `MiniStarterOpened` event.",
